# Lab Overview

This lab focuses on **joint probability**, **conditional probability**, and **relationships between random variables**. You will practice working with joint and marginal distributions, computing probabilities under conditioning, and distinguishing statistical independence from lack of correlation. You will also work with **random variable transformations**, expected values, variances, covariances, sums of random variables, and measures of dependence such as **Pearson's correlation and Kendall's** $\tau_K$. Finally, you will examine how conditioning changes a probability distribution and how **conditional independence** can be interpreted in practice. Throughout the lab, you will connect these ideas to concrete probability models and strengthen your ability to reason about multiple random variables together.

